WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.350
Jenna: If you're eager to
travel and see the world

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.840
beyond the four walls of your home,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.990
I'm right there with you.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.540
So I asked my friend
Caroline, to plan a road trip

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.910
that will dare me and all of us

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.900
to see the US in a new way.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.400
I'm Jenna Laurenzo and
this is Travel Dares

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.463
Season US.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.480
On this season of Travel Dares,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.710
I'm on a mission to find
the most interesting,

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.830
unexpected, and unique
destinations America has to offer.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.100
My first stop right here in Williamsburg,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.730
known worldwide for its
historical re-enactments

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.400
of American Colonial life.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.370
But my friend Caroline
has planned for me to see

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.500
a different side of the city,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.030
and I can't wait to find
out where we're headed.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.130
Let's give her a call.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:43.380
(phone beeping)

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.770
Caroline: Hey, how are you?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.150
Jenna: I'm good. How are you?

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.170
Caroline: I'm good.
I'm so excited for you.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.826
What is going through your head?

00:00:49.826 --> 00:00:52.610
Jenna: I'm just so excited
to go on a road trip.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.443
Caroline: Yay!

00:00:53.443 --> 00:00:55.250
Well, are you ready for your first clue?

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.040
Jenna: I'm very ready for my first clue.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.370
Caroline: Okay. So your clue
is: Commander-in-chief or bust?

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.880
Jenna: Interesting. That
sounds presidential.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.170
Caroline: It could be. It could not be,

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.150
but I'm not going to
give you anything else.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.260
I'm just gonna have you, go for it!

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.480
Jenna: Thank you so much, I'm so excited.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.125
Caroline: Awesome, Bye, Have fun.

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:18.322
Jenna: Bye.

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:21.572
(upbeat music playing)

00:01:23.338 --> 00:01:25.171
What the heck is that?

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.800
Hey!

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.040
John: Hello Jenna, How are you?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.310
Jenna: Good. This is incredible.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.020
John: Welcome to the
Ruins of President's Park.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.938
Is this the most unique
place you've ever seen?

00:01:36.938 --> 00:01:39.890
Jenna: It's the most
something, I've ever seen.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.360
John: Well come on,
Let me show you around.

00:01:42.859 --> 00:01:46.442
(mysterious music playing)

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:03.190
John: So I can tell by
the look on your face

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.200
that you've got questions.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.350
May I give you a little background,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.380
as to what you're looking at?
Jenna: Yes.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.160
John: All right. So here is
the history of this place.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.420
There was a sculptor by
the name of David Adickes

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.920
who became inspired to
create all of these statutes

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.499
after he visited Mount Rushmore.

00:02:16.499 --> 00:02:18.990
He and some others created
three sets of these.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.580
This particular set of
sculptures was in a park

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.900
about 12 miles from here
called Presidents Park.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.960
And it was functional from
about 2004 until 2010.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.660
And then another company came
in and purchased the property.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.270
The owner of the heads right now,

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.510
ended up being commissioned

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.400
to come put these in a stone crusher.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.021
Can you imagine being asked to destroy,

00:02:38.021 --> 00:02:42.460
42 beautiful sculptures of
the American US Presidents?

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.710
Jenna: That would be an interesting ask.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.972
John: That was, so
fortunately for all of us,

00:02:45.972 --> 00:02:50.720
he ended up declining and
figuring out a way to salvage them

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.390
specifically what he did you can see.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.610
All of them have holes in
the tops of their heads

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.937
Jenna: Is that how they
were transported here?

00:02:56.937 --> 00:02:59.080
John: That's what he
did is he took chains,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.570
attached them to that rebar on the inside,

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.550
hooked it up to the end of his excavator,

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.590
rocked them off of their
massive blue foundations,

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.329
put them up onto a flatbed.

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:12.560
And then strapped them down one
by one, on a bunch of tires,

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.520
and then over the course
of about three weeks

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.683
with a crew of six, he saved them.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.670
Now that you've got a
history of this place,

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.760
let me walk you around a
little bit, to give you

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.420
some individual facts about
some of the presidents.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.120
And there actually might
be a pop quiz at the end.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.386
So pay attention.

00:03:29.386 --> 00:03:31.370
Jenna: Should I, be taking notes?

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.570
John: That's not a bad idea.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.643
So Jenna,

00:03:34.643 --> 00:03:36.590
the question that always
comes up from our guests

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:39.770
is how did the owner decide to
lay them out the way he did?

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.990
You'll notice that 39 of the
heads are clustered over there.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.180
And then three of the
heads are separate here.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.350
Everybody understands and appreciates

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.230
why George Washington is there,

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.340
and where Abe Lincoln is there.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.540
But I got a lot of questions,
as to how did Andrew Jackson

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.000
made it front and center.
Jenna: Yeah

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.410
John: So I finally went to
the owner and asked him how

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.260
Andrew Jackson got the
prime spot on the property.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.570
And he basically told them because,

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.640
he has a man crush on him.
He likes the way he looks.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.270
Jenna: I like that answer.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.390
John: That's why he's there.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.380
So his nickname was Old Hickory.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:13.038
Because he was as tough
as Old Hickory. So yeah.

00:04:13.038 --> 00:04:14.150
Jenna: Quite a nickname
John: Yeah

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:14.983
George Washington,

00:04:14.983 --> 00:04:17.130
most people don't know
that he was a red head.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.163
Jenna: Wait, Hold on. He was a red head?

00:04:18.163 --> 00:04:19.087
John: He was a red head.

00:04:19.087 --> 00:04:22.050
That is not a wig. He powdered his hair.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.970
and Abe, how tall do you
think he was? Just guess

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.030
Jenna: Statuesque.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:29.420
Very much so. 6'4". My height.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.250
So he actually was the tallest
of all of our presidents.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.720
So obviously they all
have interesting facts,

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.770
associated with them all.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.250
Before we go over and talk
about the 39 heads over there.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.820
I want to bring you
over to Abraham Lincoln

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.170
and show you something really interesting,

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:43.003
All right?
Jenna: Cool.

00:04:43.003 --> 00:04:45.090
John: All right, come on over.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.300
So everybody always
asks, why Abraham Lincoln

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.060
is missing the back of his head?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.090
As that excavator was lifting Abraham

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.940
onto the flatbed to have him moved here,

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.470
he fell backwards off the flatbed.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.230
Jenna: Oh
John: What are the chances?

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.960
What are the chances? So he's the only one

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.650
that incurred damage during transport.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.300
Let me show you a couple
other things, walk this way

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.330
with me here.
Jenna: Yeah.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.250
So a couple interesting facts here

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.450
That is Gerald Ford and
what a lot of people

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.533
don't know about him is
that he was a male model.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.360
Teddy Roosevelt. Did you know

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.026
that he was fifth cousins with FDR?

00:05:19.026 --> 00:05:21.080
Jenna: I did not know that.
John: A lot of people don't.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.610
So speaking of Woodrow
Wilson, he was another

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.380
Virginia-born president,
the only president

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.400
to ever earn a PhD.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:31.133
Ronald Reagan, here he is. Remember him?

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:32.527
Jenna: He's missing an eyebrow.

00:05:32.527 --> 00:05:34.380
John: He is, he was struck by lightning.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.170
Jenna: What? In real life or the statue?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.003
John: Just the statue.

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.320
Jenna: OK well that's good to know.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.268
John: What do you think, cool?

00:05:45.268 --> 00:05:46.240
Jenna: I think this is incredible.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.050
John: Good.
Jenna: It was not a bust.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.633
John: Ooo, I love hearing it.
Jenna: It was not a bust.

00:05:50.633 --> 00:05:53.680
It was a presidential.
Should we say victory?

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.100
John: Victory absolutely.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.490
But do you remember
when you first arrived.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.422
I told you there might
be a pop quiz at the end?

00:05:58.422 --> 00:05:59.670
Jenna: Ah and there's the bust.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.473
John:Come on out. I'm going to
quiz you on a few. Follow me.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.910
Time to test your presidential knowledge.

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.197
You ready for some trivia?

00:06:08.197 --> 00:06:10.560
John: Ah yeah, let's do it.
Jenna: All right.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.501
We're gonna start with an easy one.

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:16.501
All right. What color was
George Washington's hair?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.593
Jenna: He's a redhead.
John: Boom. Nice job.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.760
Number two. This is a
little more difficult.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:26.480
I told you Andrew Jackson's
nickname. Do you remember it?

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.280
Jenna: Old Hickory
John: Boom

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.110
Jenna: That just sounded like
spice that I wanted to add

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.810
to my tea or something.
John: OK.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:35.200
Two for two. This is
kind of easy. Maybe not.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.360
I told you who the tallest president was.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.193
Do you remember who it was?

00:06:38.193 --> 00:06:39.026
Jenna: Lincoln.

00:06:39.026 --> 00:06:40.570
John: Abraham Lincoln, 6'4"

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.711
Jenna: Yes
John: Three for Three

00:06:42.711 --> 00:06:45.986
The smartest president, the
only one to ever get a PhD?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.380
You're looking in the right direction.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.920
Jenna: Is it Roosevelt?
John: Close, close.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:52.753
Woodrow Wilson.

00:06:52.753 --> 00:06:54.130
Jenna: That doesn't feel close.
John: That's OK.

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:55.863
Jenna: Doesn't even seem like it rhymes.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:03.950
I had such an amazing time
at Presidents Park today,

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.963
John, so knowledgeable, so
full of history and facts,

00:07:07.963 --> 00:07:10.210
stumped me on a few questions,

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.090
but I definitely made my
history teacher proud.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.710
It was an incredible
experience. So unique.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.400
There's nowhere in this world like it.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.930
I had no idea what I was getting into.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.380
Honestly, it's just one of those places

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.950
that you have to check out yourself.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.870
And here we go with the
clue for the next episode,

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.230
let's see. Use your fingers to handcraft

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:32.060
a piece of pre-Colonial
history. All right. All right.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:35.330
Well, we're in Colonial Williamsburg.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.460
Now we're going somewhere pre-Colonial.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:41.110
I have no idea what that
means, but I'm really excited.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:42.520
You'll just have to tune
into the next episode

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.020
to see where we're going next.

